 Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@google.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Bogdan Brinza <bbrinza@microsoft.com>"}]}},{"snippet":"Probably adding code like &quot;if this is not a click event and not a trusted event, UseCounter::","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"\"TAMURA, Kent\" <tkent@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 11 May 2016 09:54:34 +0900"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@google.com>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Bogdan Brinza <bbrinza@microsoft.com>"}]}},{"snippet":"Looking at the code I do see something problematic with https://code.google.com/p/chromium/codesearch","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 10 May 2016 20:58:09 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"From","value":"\"'Dave Tapuska' via blink-dev\" <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"\"TAMURA, Kent\" <tkent@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Bogdan Brinza <bbrinza@microsoft.com>"}]}},{"snippet":"I think this breaks the undo support in the auto complete widget used by Rietveld. https://github.com","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 10 May 2016 18:49:12 -0700"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"From","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"David Tapuska <dtapuska@google.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Kent TAMURA <tkent@chromium.org>, Bogdan Brinza <bbrinza@microsoft.com>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Is there a reason why you chose to dispatch a text input event vs calling execCommand directly?","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 11 May 2016 12:06:46 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"From","value":"\"'Dave Tapuska' via blink-dev\" <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Kent TAMURA <tkent@chromium.org>, Bogdan Brinza <bbrinza@microsoft.com>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Perhaps undo should accommodate script-entered changes as well? There used to be an UndoManager (or","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 11 May 2016 19:11:08 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"David Tapuska <dtapuska@google.com>, Kent TAMURA <tkent@chromium.org>, Bogdan Brinza <bbrinza@microsoft.com>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Another case where you must dispatch events because there is no API is to invoke a download with the","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 11 May 2016 18:46:15 +0100"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"From","value":"Ashley Gullen <ashley@scirra.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Why do you need to dispatch an event? I think element.click() should work. Besides, this intent will","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 11 May 2016 20:51:44 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Ashley Gullen <ashley@scirra.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Oh, I didn&#39;t know click() worked. Never mind then! On 11 May 2016 at 18:51, PhistucK &lt;phistuck","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 11 May 2016 18:53:59 +0100"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"From","value":"Ashley Gullen <ashley@scirra.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"To me this looks more like an intent to deprecate &amp; remove than an intent to ship? On Wed, May 11","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 11 May 2016 20:39:05 +0000"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Can we treat it as an intent to deprecate based on the discussion? I will send out a separate intent","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 11 May 2016 16:44:39 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"From","value":"\"'Dave Tapuska' via blink-dev\" <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"sgtm! On Wed, May 11, 2016 at 10:44 PM Dave Tapuska &lt;dtapuska@google.com&gt; wrote: Can we treat","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 11 May 2016 20:47:13 +0000"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@google.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Can I have a consensus to move forward on this action or not? It has been changed to an Intent to","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 17 May 2016 11:07:42 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"From","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Deprecation sounds good to me and doesn&#39;t require API owner approval. Let&#39;s discuss removal","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 17 May 2016 11:37:25 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Is there an update on shipping this? Could this possibly be just shipped without deprecation cycle","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"\"'Malte Ubl' via blink-dev\" <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Thu, 23 Jun 2016 06:58:11 -0700"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"How timely is your email.... I landed the change last night :-) https://chromium.googlesource.com/","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"\"'Dave Tapuska' via blink-dev\" <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Thu, 23 Jun 2016 10:01:05 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Malte Ubl <malteubl@google.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Fwiw removing this did break the autocomplete in Chrome&#39;s codereview tool as I said: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=632932 and execCommand doesn&#39;t appear to work on input","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 2 Aug 2016 22:41:14 -0700"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Wait, but Firefox does not fire the default action for non-click events, if I remember correctly. I guess the underlying issue (in your case) here is that Chrome does not add value changes triggered by","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 3 Aug 2016 18:48:49 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"I think this specific default action (adding to the undo stack) should just be whitelisted. Does anyone think that programmatically modifying the undo stack is harmful? And if so, why is it fine for","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 3 Aug 2016 19:03:19 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"I don&#39;t think it&#39;s acceptable to stop running execCommand against input and textarea. That completely breaks inserting text with the undo stack and was explicitly given as the workaround and a","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 3 Aug 2016 09:18:35 -0700"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, yosin@chromium.org, Ojan Vafai <ojan@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Yep, I agree that input events (textInput or the standard input) should just trigger undo stack modification. ☆PhistucK On Wed, Aug 3, 2016 at 7:18 PM, Elliott Sprehn &lt;esprehn@chromium.org&gt; wrote","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Wed, 3 Aug 2016 19:22:11 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"Elliott Sprehn <esprehn@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Jochen Eisinger <jochen@chromium.org>, Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Rick Byers <rbyers@chromium.org>, Yoshifumi Inoue <yosin@chromium.org>, Ojan Vafai <ojan@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"I agree that &quot;execCommand&quot; against input / textarea should be retained. We indeed needs &quot;void open();&quot; and &quot;void close();&quot; for &lt;select&gt; if untrusted mousedown events","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Sun, 7 Aug 2016 03:13:47 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"gongdh11@gmail.com"},{"name":"To","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"dtapuska@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"}]}},{"snippet":"In terms of the open, close etc. It was discussed that because of the really low usage of executing the default action for untrusted events. If people wanted this they could build their own custom","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"\"'Dave Tapuska' via blink-dev\" <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Thu, 11 Aug 2016 11:53:08 -0400"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: Do not perform default action on un-trusted events"},{"name":"To","value":"gongdh11@gmail.com"},{"name":"Cc","value":"blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"}]}}]},{"messages":[{"snippet":"Contacts Eng: groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org PM: laforge@chromium.org Target Q4 2016","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 9 May 2016 15:34:26 -0700"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"From","value":"Anthony LaForge <laforge@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"(Adding blink-dev) Why would YouTube need Flash? Oh, the video manager? Can you work with them in","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 10 May 2016 09:59:31 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[blink-dev] Re: [chromium-dev] Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"Anthony LaForge <laforge@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"On Tue, 10 May 2016 at 17:00 PhistucK &lt;phistuck@gmail.com&gt; wrote: (Adding blink-dev) Why would","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"Matt Giuca <mgiuca@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 10 May 2016 07:04:21 +0000"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Re: [chromium-dev] Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>, Anthony LaForge <laforge@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Sorry for not watching the slides - I am simply firewalled here, so I cannot access Google Drive","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Tue, 10 May 2016 10:07:51 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [blink-dev] Re: [chromium-dev] Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"Matt Giuca <mgiuca@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Anthony LaForge <laforge@chromium.org>, blink-dev <blink-dev@chromium.org>, Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"On Monday, May 9, 2016 at 5:35:28 PM UTC-5, Anthony LaForge wrote: Presentation HTML5 by Default","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Fri, 13 May 2016 20:21:06 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"B Galliart <bgallia@gmail.com>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"May I kindly ask what is the long term goal for the Chromium team? Will you be satisfied with this","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 00:54:02 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"\"'Ruben Gerlach' via Chromium-dev\" <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"[chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"While you may not get an official answer, it is obvious (to me, anyway) that the plan is to eliminate","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 11:07:42 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"rewb0rn@googlemail.com"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, Tommy Li <tommycli@chromium.org>"}]}},{"snippet":"Thanks for your reply. I would like to avoid a Flash vs HTML5 discussion, but let me say this: Our","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 02:10:16 -0700 (PDT)"},{"name":"From","value":"\"'Ruben Gerlach' via Chromium-dev\" <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"To","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>"},{"name":"Cc","value":"rewb0rn@googlemail.com, groby@chromium.org, tommycli@chromium.org"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"}]}},{"snippet":"Note that only the browser option will be impacted. You could still redirect your users to install","payload":{"headers":[{"name":"From","value":"PhistucK <phistuck@gmail.com>"},{"name":"Date","value":"Mon, 16 May 2016 12:58:35 +0300"},{"name":"Subject","value":"Re: [chromium-dev] Re: Intent to implement: HTML5 by Default"},{"name":"To","value":"rewb0rn@googlemail.com"},{"name":"Cc","value":"Chromium-dev <chromium-dev@chromium.org>, Rachel Blum <groby@chromium.org>, To